  "notes": "Sprint 170 P0-3 (Bug 2B / ADR-048 §Negative closure) — fix architecturally complete; 3/3 mandated TDD tests GREEN; 5 pre-existing tests in scope-blocked files now fail on literal-string assertions that hard-code the legacy `.prompt-${hex}.txt` pattern.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `src/orchestra/tmux.ts` — `writePromptFile(projectRoot, prompt, taskId)` now embeds taskId. Filename pattern is `.prompt-${taskId}-${hash}.txt`, byte-for-byte the same convention as Docker (`spawn-backend-docker.ts:227-231`). Call sites updated: `spawnWorker` passes its `taskId`; `startAuditor` passes the sentinel `'auditor'`. ADR-048 §Negative asymmetry note rewritten as a closure record (comment on writePromptFile).\n- `src/providers/claude.ts` — comment block on `_cleanupOrphanedPromptFiles` updated: removed the tmux-asymmetry caveat and recorded the closure. Filter code itself unchanged — it already handled the Docker pattern, and tmux now emits the same pattern.\n- `tests/orchestra/tmux-prompt-filename.test.ts` — 3 new TDD tests, all GREEN:\n  1. Emitted filename matches `/^\\.prompt-${taskId}-[a-f0-9]+\\.txt$/`.\n  2. Filename satisfies the selective `-${taskId}-` filter used by ClaudeAdapter cleanup (same predicate, byte-for-byte).\n  3. `_cleanupOrphanedPromptFiles(['<active>'])` preserves the active tmux worker prompt and deletes only orphans.\n\nTDD discipline observed: tests written first, RED captured (vitest output recorded 2/3 fail, 1/3 already passing because that test exercises the Docker-pattern code path which already worked), fix applied, GREEN captured (3/3 pass).\n\n## Evidence (DIRECTIVES Task 1 Kanıt)\n\n`grep \"task-\\${taskId}\\|taskId\" src/orchestra/tmux.ts | head -3`:\n  function workerWindowName(taskId: string): string {\n    return `${TMUX_WORKER_PREFIX}${taskId}`;\n   * Sprint 170 P0-3 (Bug 2B closure): the filename embeds `taskId` so it matches\n\n→ 3 matches, exceeds the 1+ match requirement.\n\nFilename pattern verified by Test 1 assertion `expect(basename).toBe('.prompt-170-bug2b-1-cafebabe.txt')`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsc --noEmit` — EXIT_CODE=0, zero type errors.\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/tmux-prompt-filename.test.ts` — 3/3 pass.\n- `npx vitest run tests/orchestra/ tests/providers/ tests/security/` — 4777 pass, 11 skipped, 5 fail. All 5 failures are pre-existing tests in scope-blocked files that hard-code the legacy filename literal in their assertions (see Tech Debt below).\n\n## Tech Debt (out of scope.filesWrite — needs trivial follow-up)\n\nFive existing tests reference the legacy `.prompt-${hash}.txt` literal in assertions. Each is a single-line update; the underlying behavior they verify is still correct, only the expected string drifted. None of these files are in this task's writable list (`src/orchestra/tmux.ts`, `tests/orchestra/tmux-prompt-filename.test.ts`, `src/providers/claude.ts`), so the writes are deliberately deferred.\n\n  1. tests/orchestra/tmux.test.ts:145 — change `'.prompt-abcdef01.txt'` to `'.prompt-task-001-abcdef01.txt'`.\n  2. tests/orchestra/tmux.test.ts:164 — change `'< /project/.tasks/.prompt-abcdef01.txt'` to `'< /project/.tasks/.prompt-task-002-abcdef01.txt'`.\n  3. tests/orchestra/tmux-edge.test.ts:192 — change `expect.stringContaining('.prompt-deadbeef.txt')` to `expect.stringContaining('.prompt-task-edge-03-deadbeef.txt')`.\n  4. tests/security/shell-injection.test.ts:50 — change `'< /project/.tasks/.prompt-deadbeef12345678.txt'` to `'< /project/.tasks/.prompt-task-001-deadbeef12345678.txt'`.\n  5. tests/security/shell-injection.test.ts:116 — change `'.prompt-deadbeef12345678.txt'` to `'.prompt-task-007-deadbeef12345678.txt'`.\n\nRecommendation: bundle these into a follow-up P1 task (or fold into Sprint 171 audit findings). Each is ≤1 LoC; total diff <10 lines across 3 files; no risk.\n\n## Honest Self-Assessment Delta\n\n- Baseline: writePromptFile = hex-only; selective filter never matched tmux; ADR-048 §Negative open.\n- End: writePromptFile = `${taskId}-${hash}`; selective filter matches both backends; ADR-048 §Negative closed in code.\n- Functional delta: ~95% (architectural fix landed and verified by 3 TDD tests). Remaining 5% is the 5-line assertion-string refresh that scope.filesWrite blocks.\n- GO_WITH_TECH_DEBT because the task spec mandates a filename pattern that breaks 5 existing literal-string assertions in files I cannot write. The fix itself is correct; the tech debt is purely cosmetic test-fixture maintenance.\n- Sprint 170 GO criterion `vitest run baseline ≥16485 pass + ≤2 fail` — this task contributes 5 new fails until the follow-up runs; if the other 2 P0 tasks introduce zero new fails, the total stays at 5 (3 over baseline). Disclosed up front for honest Brain evaluation.\n\nADR-048 §Negative §Cross-Backend asymmetry: code-level closed; documentation snapshot in `.brain/exports/decisions.md` will need a regeneration sweep on the next `deckent memory export`."
